kernel-lts (Linux 6.1 longterm kernel for Slackware 15.0)

This builds a Linux 6.1.y longterm kernel plus its modules as one
package. It starts from Slackware's own 5.15 "generic" kernel config
(the newest /boot/config-generic-5.15.* on the build machine) and fills
in options that are new since 5.15 with upstream defaults
("make olddefconfig").

It installs next to the stock kernel and never overwrites it:

  /boot/vmlinuz-lts-<version>      plus the symlink /boot/vmlinuz-lts
  /boot/System.map-lts-<version>   plus the symlink /boot/System.map-lts
  /boot/config-lts-<version>       plus the symlink /boot/config-lts
  /lib/modules/<version>/

Keep kernel-generic/kernel-modules installed as a fallback, and do NOT
replace kernel-headers: glibc and the rest of Slackware 15.0 were built
against the 5.15 headers.

Building takes a long time (from 30 minutes to several hours) and needs
about 8 GB free in $TMP (/tmp/SBo by default).

Options (set them in the environment):

  CONFIG=/path/to/config   start from this config instead
  SOURCE=yes               also package the source tree, needed to build
                           out-of-tree modules such as nvidia-kernel or
                           VirtualBox (adds about 1.2 GB)
  DEBUG=yes                keep debug info/BTF (off by default)
  JOBS=N                   parallel make jobs (default: all CPUs)

Example:
  SOURCE=yes sbopkg -V kernel-lts/15.0 -i kernel-lts

AFTER EVERY INSTALL OR UPGRADE

Like kernel-generic, this kernel needs an initrd, and the initrd holds
modules for one exact kernel version, so rebuild it each time the
package is upgraded (replace <version> with the new version):

  /usr/share/mkinitrd/mkinitrd_command_generator.sh -k <version> \
      -a "-o /boot/initrd-lts.gz" | bash

Then update the bootloader.

lilo: add this once to /etc/lilo.conf, then run "lilo" after every
upgrade:

  image = /boot/vmlinuz-lts
    initrd = /boot/initrd-lts.gz
    root = /dev/sdXN
    label = Linux-LTS
    read-only

elilo (UEFI): copy the kernel and initrd to the EFI partition after
every upgrade:

  cp /boot/vmlinuz-lts /boot/efi/EFI/Slackware/vmlinuz-lts
  cp /boot/initrd-lts.gz /boot/efi/EFI/Slackware/initrd-lts.gz

and add this once to /boot/efi/EFI/Slackware/elilo.conf:

  image=vmlinuz-lts
    label=lts
    initrd=initrd-lts.gz
    read-only
    append="root=/dev/sdXN vga=normal ro"

GRUB: run "grub-mkconfig -o /boot/grub/grub.cfg" after every upgrade,
and check that the vmlinuz-lts entry has an initrd-lts.gz line.

Upgrading the package removes the modules of the previous 6.1 version,
so reboot into the new one soon after upgrading.
